  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The eccentricity of the ellipse whose major axis is three times the minor axis is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wyDkR",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "qhRpi",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PCh0f",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xFrxI",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let a be the major axis and $b$, the minor axis of the ellipse, then 3 minor axis = major axis.\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 3 b=a$\r\n\r\nEccentricity is given by:\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\nb^{2}=a^{2}\\left(1-e^{2}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow b^{2}=9 b^{2}\\left(1-e^{2}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{9}=\\left(1-e^{2}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow e^{2}=\\frac{8}{9} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow e=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
